---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";

const EFFECTIVE = "7 November 2026";
const prose =
  "mt-8 text-[15.5px] leading-7 text-muted-foreground [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4 [&_a:hover]:text-foreground [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-muted [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[0.9em] [&_code]:text-foreground [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:text-foreground [&_li]:mt-2 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_strong]:font-medium [&_strong]:text-foreground [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6";
---

<Base
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for ui.kadal.cc: the Kadal UI code is MIT, the docs text is CC BY 4.0, the site is free and provided as is. No accounts, no payments; sponsorships go through GitHub."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.14em] text-muted-foreground uppercase">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>

    <div class={prose}>
      <p>
        These terms cover the website at <strong>ui.kadal.cc</strong>: the docs, the playground and the component
        registry it serves. The site is run by <strong>{SITE.seller}</strong>, an individual based in {SITE.location},
        trading as <strong>{SITE.tradingAs}</strong> ("we", "us"). It is free, has no accounts and sells nothing. By
        using it you agree to these terms; the software itself is governed by its licence, not by this page.
      </p>

      <h2>1. The software: MIT</h2>
      <p>
        Kadal UI, meaning the components in the registry, the examples and the <code>@kadal/ui</code> CLI, is open source
        under the <a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">MIT licence</a>. You may use, copy, change
        and sell it, in commercial products included, as long as the licence notice stays with the copies. The licence is
        the whole agreement for the code: it comes <strong>without warranty of any kind</strong>, and these terms add no
        promise to it.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The docs: CC BY 4.0</h2>
      <p>
        The text and images on this site are licensed under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>, so
        you may quote, translate and republish them with a credit to Kadal UI and a link back. Code samples in the docs
        are MIT, like the code they describe. The Kadal name and mark are not licensed: do not use them in a way that
        suggests we made, endorse or support your product.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The registry and the playground</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The registry at <code>ui.kadal.cc/r/</code> is what <code>npx shadcn@latest add @kadal/…</code> reads. It is
          provided as is; we may change, rename or remove items, and we record every change in the
          <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>. Your copy of the code is yours and keeps working whatever we do here.
        </li>
        <li>
          The <a href="/playground/">playground</a> runs code in your browser with LiveCodes, loaded from
          <a href="https://livecodes.io" rel="noopener">livecodes.io</a> under
          <a href="https://livecodes.io/docs/license/" rel="noopener">its own licence and terms</a>. What you run there
          is your responsibility.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not flood, scrape or attack the site or the registry, or use it to distribute anything unlawful. Caching the
          registry for your own builds is fine.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Sponsorships</h2>
      <p>
        Sponsorships are made through <a href="/sponsor/">GitHub Sponsors</a> and are a contract between you and GitHub
        under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/github-terms/github-sponsors-additional-terms" rel="noopener">GitHub's Sponsors terms</a>;
        GitHub bills you, and any question about a charge goes to GitHub. The perks of each tier are the ones listed on
        the sponsor page at the time you sponsor. A sponsorship is not a purchase of support, a service level or a
        licence, none of which the MIT code needs, and we do not take payment for anything on this site directly.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Contributions</h2>
      <p>
        By opening a pull request against <a href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener">kadalcc/ui</a> you agree that your
        contribution is licensed under the same MIT licence as the project, and that you have the right to contribute
        it. Issues, Discussions and the Discord follow the project's
        <a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`} rel="noopener">code of conduct</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site and everything on it are provided "as is", without warranty. To the extent the law allows, we are not
        liable for any loss that comes from using the site, the registry or the software, including lost data or lost
        profits. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
      </p>

      <h2>7. The law that applies</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at Chennai, Tamil Nadu have jurisdiction, without
        taking away any protection the law of your own country gives you.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If these terms change in a way that matters, the date above changes with them and the change is noted in the
        <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.seller}, trading as {SITE.tradingAs}, {SITE.location} · <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
